  "id": "mu",
  "term": "mu",
  "definition": "Mu is an EEG sensorimotor rhythm made up of two nonharmonic oscillatory components in the alpha and beta frequency ranges. In psychology and cognitive research, it is used as a neural marker of sensorimotor integration during speech perception and comprehension.",
